WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.350
&gt;&gt;Malcolm Grant: Ladies and gentlemen, good
morning and welcome to this meeting of the

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.879
board of NHS England here in London.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:17.500
I would like to welcome those members of the
public who have joined us in the room this

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.520
morning, and also those who are watching on
the live stream.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.600
Simply to remind everybody, it is a meeting
in public rather than a public meeting, but

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.029
it is a meeting at which the board will be
transacting substantive business.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:37.510
So, in declaring the meeting open, let me
first of all record apologies from Michelle

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:42.420
Mitchell, who is on annual leave, and to issue
a welcome to Matthew Swindells, for whom this

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.839
is the first meeting of the board.

00:00:44.839 --> 00:00:48.449
Matthew, good morning and welcome to the board.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:53.620
Declarations of interest: our current practice
is that we table a list of the declarations

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:58.079
of interest, but I invite all members of the
board to declare any further interests which

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:01.100
may involve business currently before the
board.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.640
&gt;&gt;Victor Adebowale: Just for clarity, Turning
Point runs learning disability services and

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.640
primary care.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.590
&gt;&gt;Malcolm Grant: Okay, and we have a paper
coming on learning disability.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.159
Thank you very much.

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:21.850
Any other declarations 
of interest?

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.729
No, thank you.

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:30.570
Let me take the minutes of the last meeting;
people are happy that they are an accurate

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.780
record and that I should sign them on your
behalf?

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.780
Thank you.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.450
I have no notice of any matters arising; any
matters arising?

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.690
No, thank you very much.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:47.750
For the agenda, would I please be able to
have the board's approval to reversing the

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:53.170
order of items five, that is around the MCP
emerging care model, and item six, around

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.100
general practice services, to get what I feel
is a more logical flow; are we happy to do

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.100
that?

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.190
Thank you very much.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:06.490
Let me turn to the Chairman's Report; just
two or three things that I think I need to

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:07.490
mention.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.950
The first is that this meeting takes place
as part of a series of meetings over the last

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.210
two days.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:18.480
We had yesterday the Commissioning Committee
meeting; we had a development session which

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:25.860
looked at the STP process, the outcomes and
the next steps at dementia, and at healthy

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.920
new towns.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.400
Also this morning we will be having a private
meeting which will take business which is

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.620
not, by virtue of confidentiality, appropriate
to be considered in public.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:44.110
Then this afternoon we have a meeting of the
strategic HR and remuneration committee.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:49.470
I wanted to mention specifically something
that we did yesterday, which was a ceremony

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:55.680
of awards for members of our staff who had
gone the extra mile; they were nominated by

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:04.820
their peers and we were happy to confer certificates
of award on Angela Medd, Paul Jackson, Siobhan

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:12.180
Clibbens, Vicky McAvoy, Susan Cahill[?], Becky
Burn, Siobhan Cambridge and Anita Cromer[?].

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.930
I would just invite the board formally today
to record our thanks to those who work for

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:22.420
us and upon whom we have conferred that special
recognition.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:31.090
Secondly, to record also certain changes in
the ministerial ranks since we last met.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:36.190
The team with whom we have worked in the past
include the following: Alistair Burt, who

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:43.930
announced his standing down from office before
the change of prime minister; Ben Gummer,

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:47.540
formerly our Parliamentary Undersecretary
for Quality, who is now Minister for the Cabinet

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:52.180
Office and Paymaster General; Jane Ellison,
who is our former Parliamentary Secretary

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:57.370
for Public Health, is now Financial Secretary
to the Treasury; and George Freeman, former

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.550
Life Sciences Minister, who is now based in
the Cabinet Office and becomes Chair of the

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:06.180
Prime Minister's Policy Board and Co Chair
of the Policy Unit at Number 10.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:12.180
I think I would bracket, alongside those ministerial
changes, Nick Seddon, who was the Special

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.940
Advisor on Health to the Prime Minister.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:20.041
I know the board would join me in thanking
them for their cooperation with the board

00:04:20.041 --> 00:04:25.160
in the past and our best wishes for the next
stages of their careers.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:29.400
As everybody is aware, the Health Secretary
post remains unchanged, but I should just

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:38.250
note the new ministerial line up: Philip Dunne
is the Minister for Health; his brief includes

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:44.200
overseeing all aspects of hospital care, NHS
performance and operations and other areas

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.200
of activity.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:51.190
He was previously Ministry of State at Defence;
probably a good starting point for joining

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.070
the Department of Health!

00:04:54.070 --> 00:05:01.150
Nicola Blackwood is the Parliamentary Undersecretary
for Public Health and Innovation.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.210
David Mowat joins us as the Parliamentary
Undersecretary of State for Community Health

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.940
and Care.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.600
Lord Prior remains in the department as the
Parliamentary Undersecretary of State for

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.790
Health, covering all aspects in the House
of Lords, and his brief also includes other

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.590
matters relating directly to our activities.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:26.440
Although there has been a change in the Prime
Minister and the line up of the front benches,

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:34.110
we should also, I think, note that the commitment
in the Conservative Party manifesto to implementation

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:39.660
of the Five Year Forward View remains intact,
and continues to be the basis upon which we

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:44.770
will base our discussions with the new government
team.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:51.810
Item three, just simply to record formally
that our annual report and accounts were tabled

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.870
last Thursday, together with those of the
Department of Health.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.760
That is an item that is substantively on our
agenda today, but I wanted to raise it at

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:04.090
this stage merely to invite the board to record
our grateful thanks to all of those who made

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:10.760
this possible; it is an extraordinary, complex
event to prepare the consolidated accounts

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:16.490
for NHS England and a detailed annual report,
which I believe to be a fair and accurate

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:25.160
account of our proceedings and transactions,
successes and failures over the past year.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:32.590
Fourthly, the Secretary of State tabled on
21st July his assessment of NHS England's

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:35.540
performance against the mandate.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.980
The overall assessment was a positive one.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:44.370
It observes that, in increasingly challenging
times, NHS England continued to deliver the

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:49.650
majority of our objectives in line with the
government's mandate and our business plan,

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:54.460
and that we have put key foundations in place
to deliver the Five Year Forward View.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:07:00.770
The request for the next year is for greater
progress on integration on the NHS constitution

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.430
standards and on efficiencies, and a number
of those issues are actually substantively

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.520
on our agenda this morning.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:14.840
Fifthly, to report that we had a formal accountability
meeting Tuesday this week with the Secretary

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.460
of State.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:22.810
We dealt with matters including strategic
finance update, particularly the landing of

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:31.440
the year end for 2015/16, but looking also
on to 2016/17 and beyond, and to look at the

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:36.600
review, also, of the STP package.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:45.160
Finally, two or three personal issues: one
to congratulate Victor Adebowale on the conferment

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:49.620
of an honorary degree from the University
of York.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:57.060
Secondly, to note the presence of David Roberts
on the Financial Services EU Taskforce, which

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:04.290
the Financial Times reports as an 'elite crew
to steer the City through Brexit's choppy

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.290
waters.'

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:10.860
So to have David helping to steer us through
our own choppy waters is an added advantage.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:19.479
Then, sadly, to record the death of the President
of the Association of Directors of Adult Social

00:08:19.479 --> 00:08:24.770
Services, Harold Bodmer, who sadly died of
a heart attack whilst engaged with work with

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.350
us on the STP process.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:31.650
I know the board would wish to record our
deep regrets for somebody who was a loyal

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.890
friend and a very impressive individual.

